# Never branch off a ticket

Tickets live in `docs/product/linear-tickets.md`, numbered `SHOW-1`, `SHOW-2`, and so on.

Do not create a git branch unless it is `feature/SHOW-n` for a ticket that **already exists** in that file.

A tangent, UX follow-up, or “while we are here” change stays on the current ticket branch. If that cannot work, **ask** before you create anything.

## Do not

- Name a branch after the work (`feature/add-watch-later`, `feature/fix-empty-search`, or any name that is not `feature/SHOW-n`)
- Add a ticket after the fact to justify a branch you already made
- Add a ticket so you can branch, unless this message asked you to add that ticket

## Ask first, then wait

Stay on this ticket’s branch, or add the ticket to the file first and then `feature/SHOW-n`. Do not pick for them.
